{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SM38utZRVAQTMaxuevKjxw","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tid: bb981219-65fa-4232-8768-e065ac41ab20\n3\tslug: apollo-13\n4\tname: \"Apollo 13\"\n5\ttype: area\n6\tdescription: April 1970 lunar mission aborted after an oxygen tank explosion, crew returned using the lunar module as a lifeboat\n7\tcreated: 2026-10-24\n8\tupdated: 2026-10-24\n9\taliases: [\"Apollo 13\"]\n10\t---\n11\t\n12\t## Facts\n13\t\n14\t- [stated] Launched 1970-04-11 (src: NASA Apollo 13 mission page, 2026-10-24)\n15\t- [stated] Mission goal became a safe return to Earth (was a lunar landing at Fra Mauro, changed 1970-04-13 by Mission Control abort decision) (src: NASA Apollo 13 mission page, 2026-10-24)\n16\t- [stated] Command module pilot is Jack Swigert (was Ken Mattingly, changed 1970-04-10 by KSC management meeting) (src: NASA history Apollo 13 measles article, 2026-10-24)\n17\t- [stated] Crew used the lunar module Aquarius as a lifeboat and splashed down on 1970-04-17 (src: NASA Apollo 13 mission page, 2026-10-24)\n18\t- [stated] The Fra Mauro landing site was later reached by Apollo 14 in February 1971 (src: NASA history, 2026-10-24)\n19\t- [derived] The crew swap and the explosion are unrelated: the swap was decided before launch (src: agent, 2026-10-24)\n20\t\n21\t## Links\n22\t\n23\t- commanded by [[jim-lovell]]\n24\t- crewed by [[fred-haise]]\n25\t- crewed by [[jack-swigert]]\n26\t- crippled by [[oxygen-tank-2]]\n27\t- saved by [[lunar-module]]\n28\t- investigated by [[apollo-13-review-board]]\n29\t- affected by [[rubella-crew-swap]]\n30\t- used [[co2-scrubber-adapter]]\n31\t- returned on [[free-return-trajectory]]\n32\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6366cd1-22a8-4e9d-8360-b83caa0e931a","uuid":"bde1e07f-41b9-469f-8a49-9c9823cd0111","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:27:10.329Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\shman\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-shman-OneDrive-Desktop-Yggdrass-OS-Yggdrass-OS\\4def6ebb-4bae-4ed4-85d0-92ed32e7bd0c\\scratchpad\\exp7\\brain-B\\areas\\apollo-13.md","content":"---\nid: bb981219-65fa-4232-8768-e065ac41ab20\nslug: apollo-13\nname: \"Apollo 13\"\ntype: area\ndescription: April 1970 lunar mission aborted after an oxygen tank explosion, crew returned using the lunar module as a lifeboat\ncreated: 2026-10-24\nupdated: 2026-10-24\naliases: [\"Apollo 13\"]\n---\n\n## Facts\n\n- [stated] Launched 1970-04-11 (src: NASA Apollo 13 mission page, 2026-10-24)\n- [stated] Mission goal became a safe return to Earth (was a lunar landing at Fra Mauro, changed 1970-04-13 by Mission Control abort decision) (src: NASA Apollo 13 mission page, 2026-10-24)\n- [stated] Command module pilot is Jack Swigert (was Ken Mattingly, changed 1970-04-10 by KSC management meeting) (src: NASA history Apollo 13 measles article, 2026-10-24)\n- [stated] Crew used the lunar module Aquarius as a lifeboat and splashed down on 1970-04-17 (src: NASA Apollo 13 mission page, 2026-10-24)\n- [stated] The Fra Mauro landing site was later reached by Apollo 14 in February 1971 (src: NASA history, 2026-10-24)\n- [derived] The crew swap and the explosion are unrelated: the swap was decided before launch (src: agent, 2026-10-24)\n\n## Links\n\n- commanded by [[jim-lovell]]\n- crewed by [[fred-haise]]\n- crewed by [[jack-swigert]]\n- crippled by [[oxygen-tank-2]]\n- saved by [[lunar-module]]\n- investigated by [[apollo-13-review-board]]\n- affected by [[rubella-crew-swap]]\n- used [[co2-scrubber-adapter]]\n- returned on [[free-return-trajectory]]\n","numLines":32,"startLine":1,"totalLines":32}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01SM38utZRVAQTMaxuevKjxw","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
